<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  VELVET VIKING - APPLE PRIVACY MANIFEST

  Required for App Store submission, not optional. @capacitor/filesystem's own
  README states it: an app using that plugin must declare
  NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp with reason C617.1, because the
  plugin reads file timestamps and Apple classifies that as a required-reason
  API. Valhalla does use it - canNativeShareFiles() gates the backup export on
  Filesystem and Share both being present, and nativeSaveTextFile() writes the
  export into the app cache before handing it to the share sheet.

  C617.1 is the reason Apple defines for "accessing timestamps of files inside
  the app container", which is exactly and only what happens here: the file is
  written to Directory.CACHE under this app's own container and read straight
  back. Nothing outside the container is touched.

  EVERY OTHER ARRAY IS EMPTY, AND EACH EMPTINESS IS A STATEMENT.

  NSPrivacyTracking false, NSPrivacyTrackingDomains empty: Valhalla has no
  advertising identifier, no ad SDK, no analytics SDK and no third-party
  tracker. There is nothing to declare and no ATT prompt to show, so there is
  none.

  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes empty: this manifest describes what THIS BUNDLE's
  code collects. The bundle is a WKWebView plus three Capacitor plugins; it
  collects nothing on its own account. What the PRODUCT collects - email,
  training plans, workout data - is collected by the web runtime against the
  athlete's own Supabase account, and is declared in the App Privacy
  questionnaire in App Store Connect rather than here. STORE-DATA-INVENTORY.md
  is the factual source for that questionnaire.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
      <dict>
        <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
        <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
        <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
        <array>
          <string>C617.1</string>
        </array>
      </dict>
    </array>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
  </dict>
</plist>
